# Godot 4+ specific ignores
.godot/
/android/

# local tool state (IDE / CLI), never shared
# [P66] Whole directory, per user's call on 2026-09-24: it holds only machine-local
# state (settings.local.json) and installed skills, nothing the repo should carry.
.qoder/
.marscode/

# [P95] The headless verification sandbox: `XDG_DATA_HOME=<repo>/.xdgtest` keeps the
# probes' user:// writes inside the workspace, and every run drops a log there.
# Machine-local test state - never committed.
.xdgtest/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# [repo-slim] External assets: large binaries authored/procured outside the repo.
# The code references them by file name (balance_audio.gd track/cue tables, ui_font.gd
# scans the font dir); a clone without them degrades to no sound / CJK fallback to
# English, it does NOT break the build. They are NOT deterministic build inputs and
# MUST NOT be packed into git. Only the human-written asset manifests are tracked
# (assets/audio/readme.md lists the 173 wav cues; docs describe how to supply them).
*.wav
*.mp3
*.ogg
assets/fonts/*.ttf
assets/fonts/*.otf
assets/fonts/*.woff
assets/fonts/*.woff2

# [repo-slim] Godot import metadata is regenerated by the editor on import
# (deterministic from the source asset + .godot/). It carries no hand-made edits.
# Keeping it tracked would re-introduce the very assets we just externalised.
# *.import = asset import sidecars; *.uid = per-script Godot 4 UIDs (uid://...),
# both recreated by `godot --headless --import`, neither carries hand-made edits.
*.import
*.uid

# [repo-slim] Downloadable third-party plugin (NOT first-party source).
# addons/curved_lines_2d = "Scalable Vector Shapes 2D" v2.34.5 (MIT,
# see its plugin.cfg). It is fetched from the Godot ecosystem, not written here.
# NOTE: 5 unit view scenes reference its .gd via ext_resource:
#   scenes/units/plants/{peashooter,blaze_pepper,pepperking,spikerock}_view.tscn
#   scenes/units/humans/human.tscn
# a clone without the plugin FAILS TO LOAD those scenes until the plugin is
# re-acquired. Version + consequences are pinned in README.md / docs/STATE.md.
addons/

# [repo-slim] Historical archive = "what happened then", not current truth.
# docs/history/ (P0-P27, P28, P37-P82, P83-P110, brawl B1-B22) is session/phase
# narration, not first-party source. Local-only, NOT packed into git.
# Live docs still quote it as "see <history file> §N" - those are KNOWN DEAD LINKS
# in a public clone (explicitly marked in AGENTS.md / docs/INDEX.md / README.md).
# scripts/core/doc_check.gd skips its archive claims when this dir is absent.
docs/history/
